## Why This Is Asked
This tests mastery of DAG shortest paths and cross-checks understanding of BFS/DFS-derived ordering vs Dijkstra's heap-based approach.

## Key Concepts
- Topological sort (DFS or Kahn)
- DAG single-source shortest paths via DP
- Edge relaxation and cycle detection

## Code Example
```javascript
function dagSSSP(n, edges, s){
  const g=[...Array(n)].map(()=>[]);
  const indeg=new Array(n).fill(0);
  for(const [u,v,w] of edges){g[u].push([v,w]); indeg[v]++;}
  const q=[]; for(let i=0;i<n;i++) if(indeg[i]===0) q.push(i);
  const topo=[]; while(q.length){ const u=q.shift(); topo.push(u); for(const [v] of g[u]){ if(--indeg[v]===0) q.push(v);} }
  const INF=1e15; const dist=new Array(n).fill(INF); dist[s]=0;
  for(const u of topo){ if(dist[u]===INF) continue; for(const [v,w] of g[u]) dist[v]=Math.min(dist[v], dist[u]+w);} 
  return dist;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you modify for multiple sources? 
- How would you handle cycles or return -1 when unreachable?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of Trie data structures, deduplication strategies, and efficient prefix queries—essential skills for building autocomplete systems.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node subtree counts for O(1) prefix counting
- Deduplication via global set to maintain word uniqueness
- Prefix-based retrieval with controlled result limits
- Lexicographic ordering through systematic child traversal

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.next = new Map();
    this.isWord = false;
    this.passCount = 0;
  }
}

class Trie {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
    this.wordSet = new Set();
  }

  insert(word) {
    if (this.wordSet.has(word)) return;
    this.wordSet.add(word);
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of word) {
      if (!node.next.has(char)) {
        node.next.set(char, new TrieNode());
      }
      node = node.next.get(char);
      node.passCount++;
    }
    node.isWord = true;
  }

  countPrefix(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      if (!node.next.has(char)) return 0;
      node = node.next.get(char);
    }
    return node.passCount;
  }

  listWithPrefix(prefix, limit) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const char of prefix) {
      if (!node.next.has(char)) return [];
      node = node.next.get(char);
    }
    const result = [];
    this.dfs(node, prefix, result, limit);
    return result;
  }

  dfs(node, current, result, limit) {
    if (result.length >= limit) return;
    if (node.isWord) {
      result.push(current);
    }
    const sortedKeys = Array.from(node.next.keys()).sort();
    for (const char of sortedKeys) {
      this.dfs(node.next.get(char), current + char, result, limit);
    }
  }
}
```
